BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Cape Canaveral's ground</h1>
The ground about Cape Canaveral is flat coastal land a few metres above
the sea; its elevation data are a surface model (tree canopy, buildings).
The ground the physics and the meshes share must be bare earth there:
no spikes or bumps along the runways and their approaches, nor out to
the horizon; the runways' graded strips flush with the ground about them;
the levels the physics reads at different heights in agreement. Needs
Earth's elevation data (skipped without it).
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
